From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] wineumpd.drv, gdi32: a program's printer DC measures the printer's Windows driver's device

gdi32 opened every printer DC through our PostScript driver, whose page
comes from a PPD: with a maker's driver the program laid its page out for a
different device than the driver prints. A printer whose driver is not the
PostScript driver is now opened through wineumpd.drv, which asks the driver
what the device measures (DrvEnablePDEV's GDIINFO: resolution, printable
area and offset, the sheet) and makes a DC that answers GetDeviceCaps with
it; gdi32 still records the pages for the print processor. A 32-bit program
with a 64-bit driver gets the measurements from our 64-bit host.

Test: test/printdrv-gate.sh, 64- and 32-bit (mutant SG_MUTANT_UMPDDC).
